# The published image is NOT usable here.
#
#   docker pull ghcr.io/flexprice/flexprice:v2.1.48
#   -> Error response from daemon: error from registry: unauthorized
#
# `ghcr.io/flexprice/flexprice` is published by `.github/workflows/publish-app-image.yml`
# (IMAGE_NAME = ${{ github.repository_owner }}/flexprice, multi-arch amd64+arm64,
# cosign-signed, Trivy-gated, label AGPL-3.0-only) but the package is private:
# anonymous token requests get UNAUTHORIZED and there is no Docker Hub image
# (hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/flexprice/flexprice -> 404). So `compose.yaml`
# builds from this checkout instead. That is what upstream's own docker-compose.yml
# does too (`image: flexprice-app:local`, built from the local Dockerfile), so we
# are not doing anything they do not.
#
# Consequence for the AGPL memo's "pin by digest" discipline: for a locally built
# image the pin is the commit above plus the image ID below, recorded after the
# build. It is NOT a registry digest, and no `:latest` is involved.
